.TH WELLUP 1 "August 2026" "wellup 1.0" "wellutils"
.SH NAME
WellUp \- checks for available system updates and applies them automatically
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wellup
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wellup
.PP
Detects the system's package manager from
.BR /etc/os-release
and lists the available package updates, then applies them automatically.
By default the update is started after a short countdown so it can be
interrupted with Ctrl+C.  Supported package managers: pacman (Arch),
dnf (Fedora/RHEL), apt (Debian/Ubuntu/Bodhi), zypper (openSUSE),
apk (Alpine), xbps (Void) and emerge (Gentoo).
.PP
When stdout is a terminal the output is drawn as a box; when piped a plain layout is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " ru|en|auto"
Force report language (default \fBauto\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-color " always|never|auto"
Force, disable, or auto-detect ANSI colour.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Plain text output without box drawing.
.TP
.B \-\-box
Force box drawing even when piped.
.TP
.B \-\-no-emoji
Disable emoji icons.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable JSON on stdout; errors still go to stderr.  JSON mode
never installs anything; it only reports the available updates.
.TP
.BR \-\-check ", " \-\-list
Only list the available updates; do not install them.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose tracing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (including \fB\-\-check\fR and \fB\-\-json\fR).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage.
.TP
.B 3
Unexpected runtime error (no supported package manager, or the update failed).
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted during the update countdown.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WELLUTILS_LANG
\fBru\fR or \fBen\fR; overrides locale detection.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables colour in auto mode.
.SH AUTHOR
wellbou_
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wellutils (1)
